          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582783,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Early Life</strong><br>\nDavid Ben-Gurion was born as David Grün in Płońsk, Poland. In his youth, he joined a Zionist youth movement, dreaming of a Jewish state. He moved to Palestine in 1906, which was then part of the Ottoman Empire, and worked as a farmer. His early experiences shaped his lifelong commitment to Zionism, the movement for the creation of a Jewish homeland in Palestine.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Zionist Activity</strong><br>\nBen-Gurion became a leader in the Zionist movement. He advocated for Jewish self-defense and the Hebraization of the Jewish settlers' names as a symbol of a new identity. During World War I, he was deported by the Ottoman authorities for his Zionist activities but continued his efforts abroad, returning to Palestine after the war.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Political Career</strong><br>\nAfter the war, Ben-Gurion played a key role in establishing the Histadrut, the General Federation of Laborers in the Land of Israel. His leadership in the Jewish community in Palestine grew, and he became a prominent figure in the Zionist Executive Committee. He worked tirelessly for Jewish settlement and labor rights.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "53bc5361-5ce5-43a9-a00f-57bbceee9cd0"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
            "displayAsButton": false,
            "buttonSize": "big",
            "goToSlideType": "specified",
            "invisible": false,
