          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Declaration of Independence</strong><br>\nOn May 14, 1948, Ben-Gurion proclaimed the establishment of the State of Israel. As the head of the Jewish Agency, he became the primary national leader and declared independence just before the British mandate was to end. This event marked the culmination of his efforts and the beginning of a new chapter for the Jewish people.</p>\n\n<p><strong>First Prime Minister</strong><br>\nFollowing independence, Ben-Gurion was chosen as the first Prime Minister of Israel. His government faced immediate challenges, including the Arab-Israeli War, absorbing immigrants, and building a new nation. His leadership was pivotal in establishing the state's institutions and military.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Social Vision</strong><br>\nBen-Gurion was not just a political figure but also a social visionary. He promoted the development of education and culture and pursued the ideal of making the desert bloom. His policies aimed at integrating diverse Jewish communities and developing the country's infrastructure.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
